From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thibaut Lapierre <root@epheo.eu>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/18] multinode: worker role

A worker role for multinode: `microshift run --worker` starts kubelet and
networking only, and `microshift add-node --worker` joins it.

- Workers hold no signing material: no initCerts, no CA keys, no SA keys,
  no etcd member. They take only the kubelet client CA bundle the control
  plane publishes in kube-system/kubelet-client-ca.
- They join without cluster-admin: `microshift worker-join-kubeconfig`, on
  the control plane, prints a kubeconfig with a short-lived token for
  kube-system/microshift-worker-join, which may create node CSRs (and have
  client ones auto-approved), get nodes and read that bundle, nothing
  else. The control plane applies that RBAC; the controller's kubeadmin
  kubeconfig still works as --kubeconfig.
- The kubelet bootstraps its client cert and gets its serving cert through
  serverTLSBootstrap; a kubelet-csr-approver controller on the control
  plane approves serving CSRs whose SANs match the node, and client
  renewals.
- KubeletClientCARefresh keeps the worker's kubelet client CA bundle
  current after control plane CA rotation.
- add-node removes its copy of the join credential on every exit, and
  records the control plane IP in the worker marker.
- The Kubernetes version skew policy: a worker never runs a kubelet newer
  than the control plane's apiserver. An update boot that would is refused
  before the version file is written, so greenboot rolls it back and the
  next update retries once the control plane caught up; add-node refuses
  such a join. A kubelet more than three minors behind only warns.

Layout: the worker lives in its own files, pkg/cmd/run_worker.go and
pkg/cmd/addnode_worker.go. Upstream's run.go and addnode.go only gain the
flags and one hook each, so upstream changes there rarely conflict, and
services upstream adds later stay off workers unless listed in
runWorker. Upstream's runAddNode (full etcd replica) is left unused: this
build refuses those joins.

Carried by decision, not proposed upstream.
Covered by: unit tests (CSR approver, kubelet config), multinode-test
and multinode-test (join, certs, restart without bootstrap kubeconfig).
